Third-party components
----------------------

sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), Kokoro
(Apache-2.0) and the espeak-ng data bundled with it (GPL-3.0) aren't included
either: the app downloads sherpa-onnx's official TTS build (v1.13.8) and the
Kokoro v1.0 model package from sherpa-onnx's releases on first use, checked
against their published SHA-256. Chatterbox (MIT, Resemble AI) is installed by
uv when the artist uses it; tools/voice/chatterbox_tts.py is Keyternity's own
helper. See src/voice.rs.

whisper.cpp (MIT, https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp) and its models
are not included either: on Windows the app downloads the official build
(release b5454) and the chosen model (Hugging Face ggerganov/whisper.cpp,
pinned revision), each checked against its published SHA-256; elsewhere it
uses the system's whisper-cli. See src/transcribe.rs.

FFmpeg is not included in this repository or its builds. The Windows
installer and the app download official builds from their publishers, and
the web build fetches the official ffmpeg.wasm packages; see docs/FFMPEG.md
for sources, versions and licenses.

The DragonBones verification harness (tools/dragonbones_verify) builds
against a separately obtained DragonBonesCPP checkout
(https://github.com/DragonBones/DragonBonesCPP); none of its code is
included here.

The lip-sync language modules are ported from TalkingHead's
(https://github.com/met4citizen/TalkingHead) modules/lipsync-*.mjs:
src/lipsync_en.rs and src/lipsync_fi.rs (English, Finnish and Lithuanian,
by Mika Suominen), src/lipsync_de.rs and src/lipsync_fr.rs (German and
French, by Stephan Wald), and src/lipsync_pt.rs (Brazilian Portuguese, by
Lucas Boemeke), with src/lipsync_rules.rs as their rule engine. The files
tests/data/lipsync_*_reference.tsv are those modules' output. All are used
under TalkingHead's license:

